{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"I read the roadmap in `docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md` (lines 122–181), checked `package.json`, and grepped `src/`, `scripts/`, and the docs for inline TODOs — there are none, so the roadmap is the only todo source.\n\n**Top 5, in the order the roadmap's own priorities imply:**\n\n1. **Publish `conversation-ledger` to npm, then swap the `file:` dep for a semver range.** This is the hard blocker on shipping turnbridge at all — `prepublishOnly` in `package.json:44` literally refuses to publish while the dep starts with `file:`. Deliberately deferred while both packages are dogfooded.\n\n2. **Adapter-drift automation stage 2.** `.github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml` opens a tracking issue on drift today; the commented-out follow-on job would hand that issue to a Claude Code action to revalidate the spec and draft the PR. Needs an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repo secret and comfort with CI pushing branches.\n\n3. **Close the spec verification gaps.** Large/long histories (size cliffs, Codex auto-compaction), timestamp-format tolerance, sessionId/filename mismatch, duplicate or dangling uuid handling. Revalidation tooling already exists (`npm run smoke:interactive`, `scripts/probe-codex-content.mjs`) and is the stated bar for widening version pins.\n\n4. **Multi-hop reasoning carry-over.** Reasoning replay is gated per-event on `producer.source === \"codex\"`, which today equals a per-conversation check. Reconstructing an ancestor hop's reasoning via the `continuation` lineage chain when re-bridging was explicitly deferred as a follow-up.\n\n5. **Remaining encrypted-reasoning unknowns: blob TTL, and whether API-platform-org auth behaves like ChatGPT auth.** Turnbridge replays unconditionally since auth mode isn't observable from here; a blob rejected at real `codex resume` time has no proactive detection and falls back to `--bootstrap`.\n\nOne doc nit: the roadmap still tags encrypted-reasoning replay as *